<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alegrete</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alegrete is a city in the west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul">Rio Grande do Sul</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on the Ibirapuitã River. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a> it served for a time as the capital of the Riograndense Republic, and the republic's constituent assembly met there in 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alegrete.jpg" alt="Alegrete" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Odacir Blanco · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pra%C3%A7a_GetulioVargas-odblanco.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
